CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*msm_gpiomux_recs)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct msm_gpiomux_rec)...)
#398: FILE: arch/arm/mach-msm/gpiomux.c:109:
+	msm_gpiomux_recs = kzalloc(sizeof(struct msm_gpiomux_rec) * ngpio,

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

